            <ArticleTitle>[Hemophilia B and aortocoronary bypass].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of a patient with moderate hemophilia B, undergoing CABG. Substitution therapy was realized with factor IX concentrate (Bebulin-TIM4-IMMUNO). We discuss which of the following factors: hypothermia, hemodilution of heparinisation has a substantial role in alteration of FIX coagulant activity during cardiopulmonary bypass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
